# Build-context allowlist for Dockerfile.native only (BuildKit picks up
# `<Dockerfile name>.dockerignore` ahead of a root `.dockerignore`, so the JIT `Dockerfile`'s
# context — which needs target/*.jar — is unaffected).
#
# Everything is excluded, then only what the builder stage actually COPYs is let back in. Without
# this, every build shipped ~220 MB to the daemon first (target/, .git/, .codegraph/, htmlReport/,
# .idea/ …) plus default.env and secrets/, none of which the build reads.
*

!pom.xml
!config/native.env
!certs/backbone
!src/main

# src/test is deliberately NOT allowed back in: the image build runs with -Dmaven.test.skip=true,
# so test sources are never compiled, and keeping them out of the context means a test-only change
# doesn't invalidate the (multi-minute) native-image layer.
**/.DS_Store
